ArchHub compiler (ACOMPILER)

Tree-sitter and pinned language grammars are MIT-licensed dependencies.
All transitive crate versions, source URLs, license declarations and retained
license texts: tools/archhub-compiler/THIRD_PARTY.md and licenses/.
Rustc/Clippy diagnostic, ownership and pass-registry designs (MIT/Apache-2.0)
are learned and independently implemented; no rustc/Clippy source is copied.
Ruff and Oxc (MIT), Pyright (MIT), TypeScript (Apache-2.0) are learned from
official source for bounded lexical, flow, arity and explicit-type checks.
No external Ruff/Pyright/tsc checker is invoked by the product compiler.
See tools/archhub-compiler/rules.json for exact learned source provenance.

ACOMPILER2B: bounded scope, flow and explicit call/type rules are learned from Ruff (MIT), Oxc (MIT), Pyright (MIT), TypeScript (Apache-2.0) and rustc (MIT/Apache-2.0). No checker implementation source copied and no checker executables invoked. Source/license URLs and fallback decision: evidence/acompiler2b-sources.md.

AGENTLINK2 runtime adapter shape
Source: https://github.com/nexu-io/open-design (docs/agent-adapters.md; apps/daemon/src/runtimes/defs/ and registry.ts)
